            <ArticleTitle>Trans-mediastinal herniation of bulla: Semilunar sign.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>611-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0970-2113.168128</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trans-mediastinal herniation of lung is seen occasionally but herniation of bulla across the mediastinum is rare. We report two cases with trans-mediastinal herniation of bullae leading to an unusual line appearing near the mediastinum. We propose the name 'Semilunar sign'for this radiological sign because of its resemblance to the half-moon shape.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
